<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="introduction-csp">

  <title>Introduction</title>
  <introduction>
   <p>
        Welcome to CSPossible (beta version)! Discover what’s possible when you learn computer science!
        This free course is designed to follow the College Board’s 2027–2028 AP Computer Science Principles 
        (AP CSP) revisions. You’ll learn to code using Python, explore app development with optional 
        App Inventor lessons, and explore Artificial Intelligence (AI), data, cybersecurity,and the Internet.
        With computer science, you will build skills to solve problems, think creatively, 
        and bring your own ideas to life!
     </p>

     <p>To make sure the site saves your answers on questions, please click on
        the person icon at the top to register or login to your Runestone
        course. If you are a teacher using this
        curriculum, please join the <url
        href="https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/teaching-cspossible">teaching
        CSPossible group</url> which will give you access to teacher resources.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you see errors or bugs, please report them with this <url
        href="https://forms.gle/4gMBsv4W71vG5mNe8"
        visual="https://forms.gle/4gMBsv4W71vG5mNe8">errors form</url>.
      </p>
      </introduction>
      <subsection xml:id="sisters">
      <title>Sisters Rise Up</tlte>
      <p>
       If you are a woman taking Advanced Placement Computer Science (CSP and/or CSA) and 
       identify as Black, Hispanic/Latina, and/or Native American you are eligible for a free 
       mentoring program run by Dr. Barbara Ericson at the University of Michigan. Sisters Rise Up offers weekly 
       one-hour remote help sessions and monthly two hour special sessions.  Students who enroll 
       in the program and send in their score(s) on the AP exams before the end of August 
       receive a $100 gift card.  The help sessions are led by experienced undergraduate college 
       students.  Students can start the enrollment process by providing information for a 
       parent or guardian at <url href="https://tinyurl.com/55z7tyb9">
       https://tinyurl.com/55z7tyb9</url>.
      </p>

</subsection>
<subsection xml:id="authors">
<title>Authors</title>
      <p>This course was created by Dr. Beryl Hoffman, Professor of Computer Science at Elms College, 
      MA, to follow the newest College Board AP CSP guidelines with the help of many teachers.
      Some materials were borrowed and revised from Mobile CSP, CSAwesome, and Dr. Barb Ericson's 
      AP CSP and Python 4 Everybody courses on Runestone. Special thanks to Leigh Anne Fitz of Virginia Beach Public Schools for 
      creating the solutions for teachers and for testing and debugging the beta version, Kate McDonnell 
      from Cherry Creek Schools in Colorado and Jennifer Rosato of Univerity of Minnesoto, and all of the beta
      version testers!   
      </p>
</subsection>
</section>